-- title:
--   Seminorm bounds imply continuity for additive maps between elementary Schwartz–Bruhat spaces
-- statement:
--   Let $E,E'$ be elementary groups $\mathbb R^m\times\mathbb T^n\times\mathbb Z^r\times F$ and let $L:\mathcal S(E)\to\mathcal S(E')$ be additive. Equip both spaces with the topology of Definition D.1.3.1, generated by the seminorms
--   $$\nu_{i,j,k}(g)=\sup_{a,b,x,t}|a|^j|x|^i\,\|D^kg_{a,b}(x,t)\|$$
--   (formally: the topology induced into the product over $(i,j,k)$ of spaces with uniform convergence). Suppose that for every index $p=(i,j,k)$ there are a finite set $S$ of indices and a constant $C$ with
--   $$\nu'_p(Lg)\le C\cdot \max_{p'\in S}\nu_{p'}(g)\qquad (g\in\mathcal S(E)),$$
--   stated as: whenever all $\nu_{p'}(g)\le M$ for $p'\in S$, then $\nu'_p(Lg)\le CM$. Then $L$ is continuous. This is the standard continuity criterion for maps between locally convex spaces given by seminorms, adapted to the exact uniform-convergence topology used in the formalization. It is used to check continuity of the averaging and transport operators in Lemma D.1.5.4.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, Appendix D, Definition D.1.3.1 and Lemma D.1.5.4

import Definitions.Def_MasulloGRH_SchwartzBruhat

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MasulloGRH

theorem elemSchwartz_continuous_of_seminorm_bound {m n r s : ℕ} {d : Fin s → ℕ}
    {m' n' r' s' : ℕ} {d' : Fin s' → ℕ}
    (L : ElemSchwartz m n r s d →+ ElemSchwartz m' n' r' s' d')
    (hL : ∀ p : ℕ × ℕ × ℕ, ∃ (S : Finset (ℕ × ℕ × ℕ)) (C : ℝ),
      ∀ (g : ElemSchwartz m n r s d) (M : ℝ),
        (∀ p' ∈ S, ∀ a b xt, ‖a‖ ^ p'.2.1 * ‖xt.1‖ ^ p'.1 *
          ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ p'.2.2 (elemLift g.toFun a b) xt‖ ≤ M) →
        ∀ a b xt, ‖a‖ ^ p.2.1 * ‖xt.1‖ ^ p.1 *
          ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ p.2.2 (elemLift (L g).toFun a b) xt‖ ≤ C * M) :
    Continuous L := by
  sorry

end MasulloGRH
